ssignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot v4.3.stable.mono - Windows 10.0.22631 - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3050 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6094) - AMD Ryzen 7 5800U with Radeon Graphics (16 Threads)\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10.0.22631 - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3050 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6094) - AMD Ryzen 7 5800U with Radeon Graphics (16 Threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/16215a58-381e-4be4-9f76-1bd95c1c1c9e)\n> Dir light, 45 deg. (So the light part of the sprite should at right-top side in both origin and flip-v mode.)\n> 1. Use canvas texture to set normal and enable flip_v. Works good.\n> 2. Use NORMAL_MAP to set normal and enable  flip_v. Works incorrect. \n> 3. Use NORMAL_MAP to set normal and enable flip_v in shader. Not that good since flip_v in offset is ignored. \n\n```glsl\nshader_type canvas_item;\n\nuniform bool flip_v = false;\nuniform sampler2D albe_tex : filter_nearest;\nuniform sampler2D norm_tex : filter_nearest, hint_normal;\n\nvoid fragment() {\n\tvec2 uv = UV;\n\tif (flip_v) uv.y = 1.0 - uv.y;\n\t\n\tvec3 norm = texture(norm_tex, uv).rgb;\n\tCOLOR = texture(albe_tex, uv);\n\tNORMAL_MAP = norm;\n\tif (flip_v) NORMAL_MAP.y = 1.0 - NORMAL_MAP.y;\n}\n\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCheck mrp.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[flip_mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18345373/flip_mrp.zip)\n\n","closed_by":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn",